

Going up and down the hills could be fun if it didn't make you so visible. The sudden explosion near your train gives credit to your fear. Rapidly you see were the shot was made from : a howitzer from the SRUR, with about twelve soldier around it. You don't know why they fire at you but you don't plan to stop to satisfy your curiosity. Several tracks divids later.

With a push of a button, you can decide to continue atop the hill, were you are the most visible but you know those tracks and were they lead.

You could take the one going on the opposite side of the soldiers, were you'd be out of sight. But those tracks lead to an ancient miner town, maybe filled with SRUR's soldiers waiting to capture you.

Finally, they are the tracks going through the woods of your right, clother to the SRUR's troop. You don't know much about the woods, but you know trees tend to be a thorn in the side of any long range shooter.
*let's stay on the middle track.
->Choix1
===Choix1===
The train takes Big damages
you continue on the middle track. You hear explosions all around you and the aweful screeching noice and steel against steel, shrapnels of explosive shells loudly damaging your precious train. Finally, you are out of sight, surviving the deadly encounter by a hair.
->Fin
===Choix2===
 let's go to the left track. 

You touch the switch and turn toward the abandoned miner village. You feel the tremors of an explosive shell lifting for a second the back car, but letting you continue your journey from the other side of the hill, out of sight from them cold-blooded killers. You take a big amount of damage.
A few minutes later you reach the abandoned town. No SRUR vehicles or soldiers to be seen. You continue your journey, out of harm for now.
You touch the switch and turn toward the abandoned miner village. You feel the tremors of an explosive shell lifting for a second the back car, but letting you continue your journey from the other side of the hill, out of sight from them cold-blooded killers. You take [x] damage.
A few minutes later you reach the abandoned town, to see the path blocked by a SRUR tank and about fifty soldiers, their guns pointed at you. You can't turn back, can't fight and definitively can't push that tank with your engine. Near a building there's a pile of dead bodies. Civilians. They won't negociate or take prisoners. It's the end of the road for you. 
You all die Game Over.
->Fin
===Choix3===
Let's take the right track. 
you take a deep breath and click the button. Your train goes down the tracks, ennemy fire exploding near you and severely damaging your vehicle. When you reach the forest, you are trembling, surviving by miracle. You take some damage.
You roll through the forest. You decided to slow down, the track being in bad shape and covered in mud and roots. Around the corner of a large tree, you discored to your dismay a pile of trunks disposed like a pyramid on the track. You stop the engine, and see movement among the trees...
armed mens with painted uniforms and faces come out of the bushes. One of them shout a question in Boskovian “need a hand, friends ?”.
Boskovian Autonomous Milicias ! Since the war took a bad turn, rather than traveling to join the army many brave boskovian chose to take the arms to the enemy with guerrila tactics and sabotage. The logs must be theirs.
You thank the men and informed them about the situation. They lift the logs and let you on your way.
You and the train survived...
But for how long!
->Fin
